by nicolas-grekas at 2026-10-28T01:15:49Z

I like the opt-in through the parameter type. My concern is that a parameter typed `?\Exception` receives the failure of any recoverable attribute, including a class-level `#[IsCsrfTokenValid]`. A controller that checks `$e instanceof RateLimitExceededException` and moves on otherwise would then run with an invalid CSRF token. Should broad types like `\Exception` be ignored, so that each recoverable exception has to be named in the type?

Also, the new property now sits between the `@param` docblock and the constructor, so the docblock no longer applies to it.

