by kbond at 2026-10-28T01:54:15Z

Good point, thanks. I've changed it so the parameter type has to name one of the exceptions the attribute declares, or a subclass of one. `?\Exception` and `?\Throwable` receive nothing now, so the failure is thrown as before. Unions and narrow types like `?ExpiredSignedUriException` still work. I've updated the description to match.

Fixed the docblock too.
